    "role": "assistant",
    "type": "assistant_message",
    "content": "All 19 checklist items have been tested and recorded — **17 PASS, 2 FAIL**.\n\n## Summary\n\nThe application handles the core to-do workflow and most dependency logic correctly: task creation with all fields, editing/deleting unblocked tasks, completion and view switching with accurate counts, priority and deadline sorting (undated tasks last), cycle prevention (both direct and indirect dependents are omitted from prerequisite pickers), whitespace-title rejection, and both hover tooltips (dashed connectors and prerequisite warning badges) showing dependency chains with pending states.\n\n### Failures\n\n**FT-3 — Blocked tasks are entirely uneditable.** The spec requires that a task blocked by an incomplete prerequisite keeps its description and priority editable while locking title and deadline. Instead, the edit button is `disabled=true` on every blocked task, and no alternate path (clicking the card or title) opens a dialog. The partial-edit capability is simply absent rather than partially restricted.\n\n**CS-22 — Invalid completed-and-blocked state.** After completing \"Buy groceries\" and then its dependent \"QA Full Task\", reopening \"Buy groceries\" was permitted with no warning or confirmation. \"QA Full Task\" remained in the Completed view while its card simultaneously displayed `Prerequisite \"Buy groceries\" incomplete` — the exact contradictory state the constraint forbids. The system neither blocked the reopen nor cascaded the dependent back to incomplete.\n\n### Testing note\n\nThe dashed SVG connectors (IX-18) have zero-width bounding boxes, so Playwright's hover refused them as \"not visible\"; I verified the tooltip by dispatching real `pointerover`/`pointermove` events on the Radix trigger group and confirming its `data-state` transitioned to `delayed-open`. The feature works for a real mouse (the stroke has `pointer-events: auto` and `cursor-pointer`), but the zero-area hit box is worth flagging as a usability risk."
  }
}
